00:01:09.714 --> 00:01:11.310
- You haven't slept, but
you slept one time...

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:12.754
Too many times.

00:01:12.754 --> 00:01:14.613
(laughs)

00:01:14.613 --> 00:01:17.190
- So wait, are you ready for Halloween?

00:01:17.190 --> 00:01:18.210
Like with the kiddos tonight?

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:19.080
- We can't wait.

00:01:19.080 --> 00:01:21.750
I'm a big Halloween fan, and
we always go to Kristin's house

00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:23.543
'cause she has this amazing
Halloween neighborhood.

00:01:23.543 --> 00:01:24.376
- Yes.

00:01:24.376 --> 00:01:25.209
- And so it's our tradition

00:01:25.209 --> 00:01:27.060
that we get the families
together and we trick or treat.

00:01:27.060 --> 00:01:28.290
And I also have this tradition

00:01:28.290 --> 00:01:30.720
of losing one of my children
in her neighborhood.

00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:33.619
So let's see if it goes every
year four in a row. Yeah.

00:01:33.619 --> 00:01:35.197
- But they're getting
older, so now we're like,

00:01:35.197 --> 00:01:37.230
"They're gonna want their
candy. They're gonna come back."

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.063
- [Kelly] They're gonna come back.

00:01:38.063 --> 00:01:38.896
- You know.

00:01:38.896 --> 00:01:40.260
- [Kelly] It's like dogs,
they know that you feed them.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:41.160
- [Kristin] Right.

00:01:42.204 --> 00:01:43.620
- [Kelly] Aww, they're so cute.

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:45.240
- [Kristin] I Know.
Mine's in middle school.

00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:47.160
I'm like, if you get lost
for three days since-

00:01:47.160 --> 00:01:48.150
I'm just kidding.

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:48.983
It's fine.

00:01:48.983 --> 00:01:51.030
- So wait, how's the comedy tour going?

00:01:51.030 --> 00:01:52.140
- It's going really well.

00:01:52.140 --> 00:01:54.030
We're towards the end of our third tour,

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:55.470
which is pretty crazy.

00:01:55.470 --> 00:01:57.300
- [Kelly] Yeah. That's busy.

00:01:57.300 --> 00:01:58.133
- It is busy,

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:01.020
and we have a few shows
left in the Chicago area,

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:02.820
and then we are taking a break,

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.310
and we won't tour again
until late into 2023.

00:02:05.310 --> 00:02:08.460
So we get to be home
with kids and families

00:02:08.460 --> 00:02:11.010
and then it gives us a little
time to wanna leave again.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:13.051
- [Jen] Get caught up on life,
do our Christmas shopping.

00:02:13.051 --> 00:02:14.280
That won't happen.

00:02:14.280 --> 00:02:15.113
- We won't do that.

00:02:15.113 --> 00:02:15.946
- We'll wait 'til the last minute.

00:02:15.946 --> 00:02:16.779
- We'll wait.

00:02:16.779 --> 00:02:17.612
- We will.

00:02:17.612 --> 00:02:19.530
- So wait, so for the past few Halloweens

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:22.171
we've done a digital series
that's featured some truly,

00:02:22.171 --> 00:02:26.362
truly creepy toddler stories, like this.

00:02:26.362 --> 00:02:28.862
(scary music)

00:02:30.877 --> 00:02:34.260
"When my son was two years old,
he started to name new toys

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:35.460
with the name Joe.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:38.340
Stuffed animal, dog, pet fish, et cetera.

00:02:38.340 --> 00:02:39.690
And we named all of them Joe, I guess.

00:02:39.690 --> 00:02:41.820
We thought it was an odd
name for a child to use

00:02:41.820 --> 00:02:44.220
for his pet fish, but just went with it.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:46.500
Then he had told me he
no longer wanted to sleep

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:47.687
with his stuffed dog.

00:02:47.687 --> 00:02:50.547
He told me it was because the lights play

00:02:50.547 --> 00:02:54.296
with it at night and he
doesn't like the lights.

00:02:54.296 --> 00:02:57.000
Shortly after we found
out that an old man died

00:02:57.000 --> 00:02:59.043
in our house and yes, his name was Joe.

00:03:00.930 --> 00:03:02.850
Oh no!

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:03.843
Nope. Nope.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:06.970
And that's when I move.

00:03:07.867 --> 00:03:10.080
- [Jen] Tunk! Tunk! Tunk! For sale.

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:11.518
- Yeah, no.

00:03:11.518 --> 00:03:14.910
I don't do, I'm not like
excited about that lifestyle.

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:16.440
So today with-

00:03:16.440 --> 00:03:18.480
No one is, why did I say it like that?

00:03:18.480 --> 00:03:20.970
Okay. So today with the
help of Kristen and Jen,

00:03:20.970 --> 00:03:23.190
we are bringing you
more creepy kids stories

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:25.200
sent in by moms across the nation.

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:28.110
So let's grab our flashlight
and get ready to be scared.

00:03:28.110 --> 00:03:28.943
Here we go.

00:03:28.943 --> 00:03:31.050
Jen, you've got the
first creepy kiddo story.

00:03:31.050 --> 00:03:32.250
So, and this is yours.

00:03:32.250 --> 00:03:34.200
- Well, this story's extra creepy

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:37.080
because it's my actual
daughter that did it.

00:03:37.080 --> 00:03:39.409
So a few years ago we
moved into a new house,

00:03:39.409 --> 00:03:41.857
and a few weeks in she said,

00:03:41.857 --> 00:03:44.940
"Have you seen the purple
people walking around the house

00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:45.773
Mom?"

00:03:45.773 --> 00:03:48.990
And I said, "No baby,
what do they look like?"

00:03:48.990 --> 00:03:52.920
And she said, "Well they
wear these long purple gowns

00:03:52.920 --> 00:03:54.900
and they have crowns on their head

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.060
and they're kind of see through.

00:03:57.060 --> 00:03:58.687
But don't worry," she said,

00:03:58.687 --> 00:04:00.660
"They won't do anything bad to you."

00:04:00.660 --> 00:04:02.880
I always assume that my houses are built

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:05.580
on like a sacred burial
ground or something like that.

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:07.680
And that they're cursed
'cause why wouldn't they be?

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:09.810
And I said, "Well, why
are they here baby?"

00:04:09.810 --> 00:04:14.732
And she said, "Come here.
They're here for daddy."

00:04:14.732 --> 00:04:16.477
(haunting music)

00:04:16.477 --> 00:04:18.150
- [Kelly] What?!

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:20.580
- So if anybody wants to
buy a three-two in Tarzano,

00:04:20.580 --> 00:04:22.226
I'll give you a great deal on it.

00:04:22.226 --> 00:04:23.550
(Kelly laughing)

00:04:23.550 --> 00:04:24.783
- Oh my God. "They're here for for daddy."

00:04:24.783 --> 00:04:26.040
- They're here for for daddy.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.570
- Did you tell your husband this?

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:30.624
- Yeah I told him, Yeah.

00:04:30.624 --> 00:04:32.131
- "You better look out."

00:04:32.131 --> 00:04:33.210
- Purple robes.

00:04:33.210 --> 00:04:34.797
That sound like my church choir.

00:04:34.797 --> 00:04:38.070
(audience laughing)

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:39.690
- So wait, Lonnie, you've
actually got the next one.

00:04:39.690 --> 00:04:41.280
- Oh okay. All right.

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:43.410
- Oh, work that with those nails.

00:04:43.410 --> 00:04:45.060
- Okay, here we go.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:48.097
Here's a viewer story
from a mom named Allie.

00:04:48.097 --> 00:04:50.070
"When my daughter was two years old,

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:52.860
we walked past her daycare's old garage."

00:04:52.860 --> 00:04:54.097
Sorry for the one fang.

00:04:54.097 --> 00:04:57.430
"Every day she would look up the stairs

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:00.240
of the window of the garage and wave.

00:05:00.240 --> 00:05:02.910
One day I asked her who she was waving at,

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:04.909
and she turned to me and smiled

00:05:04.909 --> 00:05:07.890
while shrugging and said, 'Pete.'

00:05:07.890 --> 00:05:10.380
I was freaked out, but let it drop.

00:05:10.380 --> 00:05:13.980
Until years later when my
son, who was two and a half,

00:05:13.980 --> 00:05:16.770
we drove by the same
window to drop him off.

00:05:16.770 --> 00:05:18.120
He'd never been there before.

00:05:18.120 --> 00:05:22.080
He looks up at the window
waves and says softly.

00:05:22.080 --> 00:05:23.086
'Hi Pete.'

00:05:23.086 --> 00:05:26.618
(haunting music)

00:05:26.618 --> 00:05:29.137
And that was the end of that daycare!

00:05:31.318 --> 00:05:34.290
- That kinda stuff, oh man!

00:05:34.290 --> 00:05:36.060
I wish you really hope it's not real.

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.740
Okay. Time for one more.

00:05:37.740 --> 00:05:38.640
This is my turn.

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:39.780
- All right. Come on Kelly!

00:05:39.780 --> 00:05:40.711
- Here we go.

00:05:40.711 --> 00:05:42.021
- Yes, yes, yes.

00:05:42.021 --> 00:05:43.110
- It's getting spooky.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:44.250
Okay, here we go.

00:05:44.250 --> 00:05:48.370
Okay. So this is weird to
see your face like that.

00:05:48.370 --> 00:05:52.620
Okay. This is from Kelly
Kimball on my staff.

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:53.453
Okay.

00:05:53.453 --> 00:05:55.890
"Charlotte, my daughter
had a bunch of friends

00:05:55.890 --> 00:05:59.820
and families over to celebrate
her fifth grade graduation.

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:02.310
Okay. As I was passing out pieces of cake,

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:05.640
I asked her friend Summer to
go count how many more pieces

00:06:05.640 --> 00:06:06.960
of cake we needed.

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:10.050
Summer comes back and
says, I think just one more

00:06:10.050 --> 00:06:13.470
unless the lady with the
red hair wants a piece.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:15.749
Bewildered, I asked her 'What lady?'

00:06:15.749 --> 00:06:18.930
And she said, 'The one in the
guest house wearing white.'"

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:20.197
What?

00:06:20.197 --> 00:06:22.830
"My mom had passed away
a few years earlier

00:06:22.830 --> 00:06:24.600
in the guest house.

00:06:24.600 --> 00:06:28.500
I showed summer a photo of my
mom and asked, 'This lady?'

00:06:28.500 --> 00:06:30.408
And she said, 'Yes.'"

00:06:30.408 --> 00:06:33.592
(haunting music)

00:06:33.592 --> 00:06:34.425
What?!

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:37.870
- That was grandma coming to visit.

00:06:39.318 --> 00:06:41.973
- I know, but should
grandma just stay away?

00:06:42.959 --> 00:06:45.783
Like I just, I just feel like
grandma should stay away.

00:06:46.710 --> 00:06:48.240
I feel like we had our time, right?

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.040
Like I, that creeps me out.

00:06:50.040 --> 00:06:51.420
Oh my gosh.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:52.350
And then a part of me is like,

00:06:52.350 --> 00:06:53.880
do you run out there to
see if you can see her

00:06:53.880 --> 00:06:54.713
and have a talk?

00:06:54.713 --> 00:06:55.546
Like what do you do?

00:06:55.546 --> 00:06:56.379
Like, I don't know.

00:06:56.379 --> 00:06:57.212
- I think you talk to Summer

00:06:57.212 --> 00:06:58.045
and you say, "Quit keeping tabs

00:06:58.045 --> 00:06:59.767
on how much cake everybody's eating."

00:06:59.767 --> 00:07:00.960
(everybody laughs)

00:07:00.960 --> 00:07:01.793
It's a party okay.

00:07:01.793 --> 00:07:03.240
- Nobody likes that person.

00:07:03.240 --> 00:07:04.073
- Yeah.

00:07:04.073 --> 00:07:04.906
- All right.

00:07:04.906 --> 00:07:07.410
And that's creepy kids
stories around the campfire.

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:09.300
